Absolute file paths go from core to the current file
Relative file paths are formated with a ./file to tell the computer to look in the current folder
../file will tell the computer go one step up in the hierarchy, going to the parent folder.

At this stage, focus on optimizing for readability rather than efficiency and the shortest number of lines.

You can access files through your editor.
with open(file) as file_name
opens a file and you don't need to remember to close it after because the actions will be indented.
"r" mode = read 
"a" mode = append (add content without removing previous content)
"w" mode = write (previous text is removed. If file doesn't exist, it will create a new file for you)

